Keyboard/mouse rotation QTEs (issue 34): while a recognized zzz-317 rotation guide is on screen, the mapped movement keys
drive one continuous full-deflection stick sweep (900 deg/s, shorter way, the guide's way when opposite, 250 ms grace
after a release) instead of digital jumps through the centre, so tapping the shown keys in order works. The held
qte_stick gesture (GOW_QTE_STICK=rotate) starts at the guide's first key and turns its way; with that assist enabled
the guide also shows the key under a circle mark. Outside a guide, keys, gamepads, evade and scripted tests are unchanged;
GOW_QTE_KEY_SWEEP=0 keeps raw keys. Whether the game rejects a centred stick was not reverse-engineered: in-game QTE
acceptance remains manual. Tests: qte_hold_test, qte_input_test (4 modes), control-prompts.

